{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "S"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 134, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv on edge 1->3 with pooling consistently lost accuracy (exps 41,42,43,48), unlike replacing weaker ops."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Dropping a parameter-free skip on edge 1->3 helped strongly (exps 84,89) while dropping a conv there usually hurt."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "With an input->output skip present, removing edge 1->3 hurt on all datasets (exps 81,83,88), leaving the output dominated by the identity path."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual input->output path where none existed gave large gains (exps 15,17), more than replacing an existing op."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing a convolution on edge 0->3 deleted useful capacity and hurt across datasets (exps 64,67,70)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty node2->output edge with a 3x3 conv adds a new computational path and was positive on all datasets (exps 74,80)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 1->3 is absent, removing edge 0->1 kills node 1's main contribution and caused large drops (exps 94,97)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv on edge 1->2 with identity removes depth on the longest path and hurt strongly (exps 52,54,58)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv on a previously empty input->node1 edge activates the deep path and gave gains (exps 24,30)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing a 3x3 conv on node2->output was often neutral-to-positive given redundant conv paths (exps 2,5,7), whereas removing 1x1/skip/pool there hurt more (exps 3,6,9,10)."}], "tok": 18870, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "none"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["none", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["none", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect"], [3, "